  "answer": "I'll look through the Shopizer cart API and how store merchant settings are read so the line-quantity limit can be enforced without a restart.The cart writes go through one facade. I'll read the store's `CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY` on each request and reject a line over that limit before anything is saved.A storefront cart line is now limited to the store's `CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY` merchant setting, or 99 when that key is missing. The value is read on each request, so a change applies without a restart. Creating a cart or adding or changing items above that limit returns HTTP 400 and leaves the cart unchanged. A quantity of 0 still removes the line.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-shop -am compile -DskipTests\", \"mvn -pl sm-shop -am test -Dtest=ShoppingCartAPIIntegrationTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\"], \"result\": \"passed\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"HTTP 400 when a line would exceed N\", \"cart left unchanged after rejection\", \"a configuration change taking effect without restart\"], \"missing\": [\"a cart API test that sets CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY and requests a quantity above that limit\"]}",
